### Logic for Calculating Requested Participations {#activity-participations-logic}

The configuration of the number of requested participations is always understood for a complete fiscal year; by default, the final number requested will be calculated pro-rata based on the number of deliveries in the membership.

This logic can be modified using [Liquid syntax](https://shopify.github.io/liquid) in the "Logic for calculating requested participations" field in [the settings](/settings#activity).

Default:

~~~ liquid
{% if member.salary_basket %}
  0
{% else %}
  {{ membership.baskets | divided_by: membership.full_year_deliveries | times: membership.full_year_activity_participations | round }}
{% endif %}
~~~

Available variables:

- **member.salary_basket**: member with a salary basket
- **full_year_max_deliveries**: maximum number of deliveries for a whole year, all cycles combined
- **membership.full_year_deliveries**: deliveries in a full year for this membership (the greater of the cycle year and the membership period)
- **membership.baskets**: deliveries of the membership period
- **membership.full_year_activity_participations**: participations requested for a full year
- **membership.started_fy_month**: month of the start date in the fiscal year (1-12, 1 is the first month of the configured fiscal year)
- **membership.started_day**: calendar day of the start date (1-31)
- **membership.basket_size_id** / **membership.depot_id** / **membership.depot_group_id** / **membership.delivery_cycle_id**: related IDs. Use `membership.delivery_cycle_id` for a winter cycle with 0 demanded participations.

`membership.baskets` and `membership.full_year_deliveries` count cycle deliveries, not persisted basket rows.

Changing the logic does not rewrite existing memberships until each one is updated, or until a delivery or cycle update resyncs them.

On a membership, "Force the annual number" skips this logic. The annual number is used as is, including for a membership that starts or ends mid-year. The choice is not copied when the membership is renewed.

Examples:

No pro-rata, use the full-year number:

~~~ liquid
{% if member.salary_basket %}
  0
{% else %}
  {{ membership.full_year_activity_participations }}
{% endif %}
~~~

Pro-rata against the longest cycle:

~~~ liquid
{% if member.salary_basket %}
  0
{% else %}
  {{ membership.baskets | divided_by: full_year_max_deliveries | times: membership.full_year_activity_participations | round }}
{% endif %}
~~~

No participations below 16 baskets:

~~~ liquid
{% if member.salary_basket or membership.baskets <= 16 %}
  0
{% else %}
  {{ membership.full_year_activity_participations }}
{% endif %}
~~~

Exempt one depot, keep the default formula otherwise:

~~~ liquid
{% if member.salary_basket or membership.depot_id == 12 %}
  0
{% else %}
  {{ membership.baskets | divided_by: membership.full_year_deliveries | times: membership.full_year_activity_participations | round }}
{% endif %}
~~~

### Signing Up for Activities

Members can sign up for activities from their member account, even if they don't have an active membership. This allows inactive members to participate in activities on a voluntary basis without commitment. They can also see the activities they are signed up for, as well as the participations they have completed and their validations.

When signing up, the member can specify the number of participants, add a note, and choose to share their phone number and departure city for carpooling. This allows a member to register multiple people at once (e.g., family members or friends coming to help). Each participant counts as one participation towards the member's required total.

<% activity_reminder_days = MailTemplate.delay_in_days_for("activity_participation_reminder") %>
If the member opts to share carpooling information, it is included in [the reminder email](/mail_templates/activity_participation_reminder), sent <%= activity_reminder_days %> days before the activity, alongside the contact details of the other participants who also opted in. The delay is set on that email.

A sign-up deadline (in days) before the activity date can be defined in [the settings](/settings#activity) to avoid last-minute registrations.

A cancellation deadline (in days) can also be defined in [the settings](/settings#activity). After this deadline, members will no longer be able to cancel their registration themselves — only an admin can cancel it on their behalf.

## Activities {#activities}

You can create activities from [the activities list](/activities) by clicking on "New activity". As with deliveries, you can easily create activities in bulk using the "Multiple dates" tab in [the creation form](/activities/new).

> If you often offer similar activities at the same location, consider creating ["activity templates"](/activity_presets) to save time.

### Hidden Activities

Activities can be marked as "not visible" in the activity form. Hidden activities will not appear in the member's sign-up calendar, but admins can still manually assign members to them. When a member is assigned to a hidden activity, it will appear normally in their list of coming and past participations.

This is useful for activities that are invitation-only or reserved for specific members.

## Participations {#participations}

Activity sign-ups made by members are visible from [the participations list](/activity_participations). Admins can also manually sign up members or modify/delete existing participations.

Participations in activities (of the same day or past) can be validated or rejected by admins. Members will then receive an email [of confirmation](/mail_templates/activity_participation_validated) or [of rejection](/mail_templates/activity_participation_rejected) of their participation.

- **Validate**: The member showed up and completed the activity. The participation counts towards their required total.
- **Reject**: The member did not show up or left early. The participation does not count, and the activity slot becomes available again for other members to sign up.

To validate or reject participations, you can either use the batch actions from [the participations list](/activity_participations?scope=pending) (select one or more participations, then choose the action), or use the action buttons directly from a pending participation's detail page.

## Billing {#billing}

The price adjustment is calculated from the demanded participation count on the membership. Validating extra work does not change it.

If a price is defined for a participation, you can bill missing participations from [the participations list](/activity_participations). Each billed participation is then counted as validated.

More information on [billing participations](/handbook/billing#activity) is available in the billing handbook.
